  "identityConclusions": {
    "482": "Kebili inhabited-city usage and the Janoura entrance are independently identified by the Interior Ministry. The exact authentic town and existing Arabic/French city-named reference support one display choice, preserving the accepted Janoura/Sud context despite both coordinates being geometrically Nord.",
    "600": "Accept only the narrow Arabic settlement interpretation of existing reference600: its Arabic name صيادة identifies Sayada town, and both retained coordinates lie in Sayada Est. The official Monastir geography document names Sayada separately from Lamta and Bou Hjar; this supports the town identity and explicitly prevents treating the three settlements or their compound delegation as equivalent. Existing French/English Sayada Lamta Bouhjar labels remain byte-exact legacy reference labels.",
    "624": "The official municipal city-name usage, municipal civic address and exact authentic town record support Tataouine city identity. The city display association spans distinct retained source contexts: node in South and base in North. Neither reparenting nor a common-delegation containment claim is supported."
  },
  "requiredSourceProofFacts": [
    "Exact current target/base objects, three authentic node payloads and original/effective complete name-peer inventories.",
    "All53 official imadas,64 current raw records and every complete typed group; retain the eight existing non-singleton imada groups and their polygon/point members.",
    "Explicit positive and negative membership for each source delegation and common governorate, distinguishing geometric membership from existing administrative_context effects.",
    "Preserve and bind every existing name_tags, preserve_point, manualPointId, administrative_context and Chenini official replacement in its actual processing order; no fabricated boundary-only lineage for name changes.",
    "Explicit Sayada Arabic settlement identity and unchanged compound Latin labels, with separate Lamta and Bou Hjar imadas/groups.",
    "Only three target pickerGroupId fields; no name/kind/coordinate/default/context/boundary/tiny changes; preserve both Tataouine localRecords and all existing guards."
  ],
